{"availability":"available","full":"featherless-ai/simple-jev","name":"simple-jev","description":"Turn any open model into a classifier/jev endpoint","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":605,"forks":70,"created":"2026-09-18T09:52:15Z","updated":"2026-10-07T22:54:59Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://simple-jev-demo-api.featherless.ai/v1/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:05.293Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:05.293Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:05.293Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T09:01:27.759Z","stars":599,"forks":69},{"at":"2026-10-15T13:02:05.293Z","stars":605,"forks":70}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Use compatible open models from huggingface, for structured classification and scoring, without training a separate classifier head.","Explore the demos, playground, and documentation at simple-jev.featherless.ai.","Send shared context and a set of questions. Simple Jev reads the model's next-token logits for each question and builds a JSON response containing choices, rubric scores, or truth/support judgments. The model does not generate a JSON completion: the server constructs the response from the scores."],"features":["The shared prompt builder creates consistent classifier instructions and one scoring branch per question.","The HF server renders those instructions and the context into the model's native chat format.","It evaluates the exact common token prefix once and reuses that prefix's KV cache across batches of question suffixes.","It reads the next-token logits for the allowed answer labels. Shared scoring code normalizes those scores and constructs the JSON response."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/featherless-ai/simple-jev/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1cf1086ca6564b2ed323fafff5970930abe62c3884d8e1b989cb8be01423730f","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:25.747Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-